{"parentUuid":"3ee3d54c-8824-41aa-9a6e-1d659d9ddbe1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HgfETbwBR5k3eHJKNXgL7c","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Z3 SMT solver 2025 latest version features release notes\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"z3/RELEASE_NOTES.md at master · Z3Prover/z3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/blob/master/RELEASE_NOTES.md\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · Z3Prover/z3\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/z3prover/z3/releases\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Z3Prover/z3: The Z3 Theorem Prover · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3\"},{\"title\":\"z3-solver · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/z3-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Programming Z3\",\"url\":\"https://theory.stanford.edu/~nikolaj/programmingz3.html\"},{\"title\":\"12 Solving SAT and SMT Problems Using Z3\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.umd.edu/class/fall2025/cmsc433/Solving_SAT_and_SMT_Problems_Using_Z3.html\"},{\"title\":\"Home · Z3Prover/z3 Wiki · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/z3prover/z3/wiki\"},{\"title\":\"Discussing “Z3: An Efficient SMT Solver” – The Updated Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://blogs.fediscience.org/the-updated-scholar/2025/09/15/discussing-z3-an-efficient-smt-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Lessons Learned With the Z3 SAT/SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.johndcook.com/blog/2025/03/17/lessons-learned-with-the-z3-sat-smt-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Z3 - Microsoft Research: Downloads\",\"url\":\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/project/z3-3/downloads/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about Z3 SMT solver's latest version and features:\n\n## Latest Version\n\nThe latest version of Z3 is 4.16.0.0, released on February 19, 2026.\n\n## Recent Features and Release Notes\n\nSeveral notable features have been added in recent releases:\n\n**Parallel Solving:** A new algorithm for smt.threads=k (where k > 1) uses a shared search tree.\n\n**User Propagator Enhancements:** A UserPropagator callback option was added for quantifier instantiations, allowing the user propagator to intercept quantifier instantiations and inspect them in the callback, with the ability to signal whether instantiations should be discarded or delayed.\n\n**Integer Arithmetic Improvements:** Improved integer cut algorithms for linear integer arithmetic that integrate diophantine equation solving with stronger cuts.\n\n**Initial Value Setting:** The solver can attempt to use initial values in the initial phase of search, aimed at resolving nearly similar problems or problems with a predicted model.\n\n**API Additions:** New SMTLIB2 API functions ubv_to_int, sbv_to_int, and int_to_bv were added.\n\n**Bug Fixes:** Multiple bug fixes have been implemented, including fixing a memory leak in undo_fixed_column when handling big number cleanup and fixing NuGet packaging to handle dynamic glibc versions across different Linux distributions.\n\nFor comprehensive details, you can check the official release notes on the [Z3 GitHub repository](https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/blob/master/RELEASE_NOTES.md).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"204a588f-b55f-4771-96e7-f4c4bd802d62","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:18.010Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ee3d54c-8824-41aa-9a6e-1d659d9ddbe1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"11c9d2eb-4f3f-411d-ab0e-a2c3ae0e2796","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UdbPN4BPAhyE3ogapTLWDV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cvc5 1.2 1.3 release 2025 SMT solver linear integer arithmetic\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cooperating Techniques for Solving Nonlinear Real Arithmetic in the cvc5 SMT Solver (System Description) | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-10769-6_7\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/publications/2022/BarbosaBBKLMMMN-TACAS22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Theory of Linear Arithmetic — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.0/examples/lineararith.html\"},{\"title\":\"Cooperating Validity Checker - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooperating_Validity_Checker\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/359546891_cvc5_A_Versatile_and_Industrial-Strength_SMT_Solver\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-99524-9_24\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://homepage.divms.uiowa.edu/~ajreynol/tacas22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · cvc5/cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5/releases/\"},{\"title\":\"FM Artifact Evaluation Available FM Artifact Evaluation Reusable\",\"url\":\"https://hanielbarbosa.com/papers/fm2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Algebraic Reasoning Meets Automata in Solving\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.18995\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about cvc5 and its handling of linear integer arithmetic, though the results primarily discuss versions 1.0 and earlier rather than specific 1.2 or 1.3 releases in 2025.\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**cvc5 and Linear Integer Arithmetic:**\ncvc5 is an SMT solver in the Cooperating Validity Checker (CVC) family, with cvc5 being the latest major version. cvc5 is more permissive than the SMT-LIB standard and allows mixing integers and reals in linear sums.\n\n**Linear Arithmetic Support:**\ncvc5's nonlinear arithmetic solver first checks input assertions by the linear arithmetic solver, where they are linearized implicitly by treating every application of multiplication as if it were an arithmetic variable.\n\n**Version Information:**\nThe search results show references to cvc5 version 1.0.5 in a 2024 academic paper, but I did not find specific information about versions 1.2 or 1.3 scheduled for 2025 in these results. The GitHub releases page appears to have recent release notes but the specific version numbers and 2025 release dates for versions 1.2 and 1.3 are not detailed in the search results provided.\n\nIf you need information about specific upcoming releases of cvc5 1.2 and 1.3 scheduled for 2025, I would need to search more specifically for recent cvc5 release announcements or roadmap documents.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8cc45f16-0d0a-4ce2-9ca3-d442ad9271e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:18.442Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11c9d2eb-4f3f-411d-ab0e-a2c3ae0e2796","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"68af86b8-ed78-429b-8566-7948738881d4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NVNSGUt7XjXtEqz7dbEBYQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMT solver vs CP-SAT placement packing 2D rectangle benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Differential cryptanalysis with SAT, SMT, MILP, and CP\",\"url\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/105.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking/README.md at master · johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking: 2D Strip Packing problem solved with different approaches\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/johnMinelli/CP-SAT-SMT_2D-StripPacking\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluating SAT and SMT Solvers on Large-Scale Sudoku Puzzles\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.08569v1\"},{\"title\":\"Performance comparison between SMT solvers Z3 and OptiMathSAT and MILP... | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Performance-comparison-between-SMT-solvers-Z3-and-OptiMathSAT-and-MILP-solver-Gurobi-over_fig3_329612297\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"SMT vs SAT\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/picat-lang/c/in7GMF3Bd_o\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A SAT-based Method for Solving the Two-dimensional Strip Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220445013_A_SAT-based_Method_for_Solving_the_Two-dimensional_Strip_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"2D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/gMgPBryj1wA\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding SMT solvers versus CP-SAT for 2D rectangle placement and packing:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nGoogle's CP-SAT solver takes more than 300 seconds to solve single 2D orthogonal packing problem (OPP) subproblems, and some cannot be solved even with far greater time limits.\n\nThe 2D strip packing problem has been solved with constraint programming implementation and with SAT solver approaches both in constrained SAT formulation and in the more expressive SMT formulation.\n\n## General Performance Patterns\n\nSometimes SMT (especially the Z3 solver) is faster for smaller instances but often SAT is then faster for larger problems.\n\nFor scheduling problems more generally, each solver excels for certain types of problems; the MILP solver generally performs better when the problem is highly constrained or infeasible, while the SMT solver performs better otherwise.\n\n## CP-SAT Practical Implementation\n\nUsing Google OR-Tools CP-SAT with the AddNoOverlap2D function for 2D bin packing can solve problems in about 0.5 seconds on a laptop, though this depends significantly on problem size and complexity.\n\nThe search results indicate there are active projects comparing these approaches for 2D rectangle packing, including GitHub repositories with implementations, but the relative performance appears to be problem-dependent rather than showing clear universal superiority of one approach over another.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"983760b6-8ebd-4353-b177-d5d8e6baf811","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:19.014Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"68af86b8-ed78-429b-8566-7948738881d4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3efbeac0-63d1-4f56-b8cd-c37f8d4cab4b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KZnsvgWdhfrkEDjeCTGb9i","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMT-COMP 2025 results QF_LIA QF_NIA winners benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SMT-COMP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/\"},{\"title\":\"Local Search For Satisfiability Modulo Integer Arithmetic Theories | ACM Transactions on Computational Logic\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3597495\"},{\"title\":\"Qf_slia Single Query | SMT-COMP\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2023/results/qf-slia-single-query\"},{\"title\":\"SMT-COMP 2023 18th International Satisfiability Modulo Theory Competition\",\"url\":\"https://smt-workshop.cs.uiowa.edu/2023/slides/smtcomp.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SMT-COMP | The International Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT) Competition.\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2023/benchmarks.html\"},{\"title\":\"SMT-LIB The Satisfiability Modulo Theories Library\",\"url\":\"https://smt-lib.org/news.shtml\"},{\"title\":\"Satisﬁability Modulo Theories: A Beginner’s Tutorial Clark Barrett1(B)\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10584608\"},{\"title\":\"| SMT-COMP 2024\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2024/results/largest-contribution-single-query/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SMT-COMP: Satisfiability modulo theories competition\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/225778702_SMT-COMP_Satisfiability_modulo_theories_competition\"},{\"title\":\"SMT-COMP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2025/\"}]\n\nI found that SMT-COMP 2025 results are available as of August 11, 2025. Let me search more specifically for the detailed results for the QF_LIA and QF_NIA divisions.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lia Single Query - SMT-COMP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2022/results/lia-single-query\"},{\