{"parentUuid":"11892f48-2ee4-4c3a-b20a-57d2eb30c243","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Request failed with status code 404","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QbBX5GCn6jsuubz7cmQaRy"}]},"uuid":"2e45efe3-057a-461d-ad75-aaa8ff43ef43","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:44.088Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Request failed with status code 404","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11892f48-2ee4-4c3a-b20a-57d2eb30c243","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ea47b2f5-cc3d-4aed-9e20-cfceccbcbbba","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016WzSqk16E77qM59P3QGqzF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Yices2 SMT solver Python binding linear integer arithmetic 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - SRI-CSL/yices2: SRI Yices SMT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SRI-CSL/yices2\"},{\"title\":\"The Yices SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://yices.csl.sri.com/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - BrunoDutertre/yices2: The Yices SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/BrunoDutertre/yices2\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SeanRBurton/yices2: The Yices SMT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SeanRBurton/yices2\"},{\"title\":\"Release Notes - Yices\",\"url\":\"https://yices.csl.sri.com/release-notes.html\"},{\"title\":\"Yices 2 in SMT-COMP 2021 Bruno Dutertre, Dejan Jovanovi´c,\",\"url\":\"https://smt-comp.github.io/2021/system-descriptions/Yices2.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"FreshPorts -- math/yices: SMT solver\",\"url\":\"https://www.freshports.org/math/yices\"},{\"title\":\"July 16, 2025 Yices Manual Version 2.7.0 Bruno Dutertre\",\"url\":\"https://yices.csl.sri.com/papers/manual.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"yices2/README.md at master · SRI-CSL/yices2\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SRI-CSL/yices2/blob/master/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Shae Erisson's blog - Part two of SMT Solvers, Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://shapr.github.io/posts/2019-07-12-smt-solvers-part-two.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Yices2 SMT solver with Python bindings and linear integer arithmetic:\n\n## Yices2 SMT Solver Overview\n\nYices 2 is an SMT solver that decides the satisfiability of formulas containing uninterpreted function symbols with equality, real and integer arithmetic, bitvectors, scalar types, and tuples. Yices 2 supports both linear and nonlinear arithmetic.\n\n## Python Bindings\n\nThe solver provides bindings for Java, Python, Go, and OCaml. Yices currently provides wrappers to the Yices API for Python, Java, Go and OCaml. Python bindings were improved and moved to a git submodule.\n\n## Recent Updates (2025)\n\nThe latest release was on July 16, 2025. The official manual available is for Version 2.7.0, which covers the Python API and other language bindings.\n\n## Linear Integer Arithmetic Support\n\nFor linear integer arithmetic specifically, Yices2 supports the QF_LIA (Quantifier-Free Linear Integer Arithmetic) logic as part of its comprehensive set of supported theories.\n\nThe source code and documentation are available on the official GitHub repository (https://github.com/SRI-CSL/yices2).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"29371726-eb83-4ccc-9016-e5333c6dc0b6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:47.365Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ea47b2f5-cc3d-4aed-9e20-cfceccbcbbba","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f3a569d1-3917-47c9-b77f-15bda3d39341","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNcwH7T3aCsYD9PwVHTaDK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PySMT library unified abstraction Z3 cvc5 yices comparison\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver⋆ Haniel Barbosa3\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/publications/2022/BarbosaBBKLMMMN-TACAS22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Add SMT abstraction · Pull Request #581 · Consensys/mythril\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Consensys/mythril/pull/581\"},{\"title\":\"Getting Started — pySMT 0.9.7 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysmt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/getting_started.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysmt/pysmt: pySMT: A library for SMT formulae manipulation and solving · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysmt/pysmt\"},{\"title\":\"PySMT · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/PySMT/\"},{\"title\":\"Change Log — pySMT 0.9.7 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysmt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/CHANGES.html\"},{\"title\":\"SMTMSMT: Gluing Together CVC5 and Z3 Nelson Oppen Style | Hey There Buddo!\",\"url\":\"https://www.philipzucker.com/glue-cvc5-z3/\"},{\"title\":\"FM Artifact Evaluation Available FM Artifact Evaluation Reusable\",\"url\":\"https://hanielbarbosa.com/papers/fm2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver | Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-030-99524-9_24\"},{\"title\":\"JavaSMT 3: Interacting with SMT Solvers in Java | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-81688-9_9\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about PySMT's unified abstraction for SMT solvers:\n\n## PySMT Overview\n\nPySMT provides a unified API for SMT-lib compatible constraint solvers including Z3, CVC4, Yices, etc. PySMT works with any SMT-LIB compatible solver and can leverage the API of the following solvers: MathSAT, Z3, cvc5, Yices 2, CUDD, PicoSAT, and Boolector.\n\n## Key Features\n\npySMT provides methods to define a formula in Linear Real Arithmetic (LRA), Real Difference Logic (RDL), Equalities and Uninterpreted Functions (EUF), Bit-Vectors (BV), Arrays (A), Strings (S) and their combinations.\n\n## Solver Support Comparison\n\nThe supported theories vary across solvers: MathSAT supports UF, LIA, LRA, BV, AX; Z3 supports UF, LIA, LRA, BV, AX, NRA, NIA; cvc5 supports UF, LIA, LRA, BV, AX, S; Yices supports UF, LIA, LRA, BV; and Boolector supports UF, BV, AX.\n\n## Benefits of Unified Abstraction\n\nFrameworks that provide a unified API to SMT solvers (such as JavaSMT, PySMT, and ScalaSMT) are necessary because the characteristics of the SMT solvers vary a lot. With pySMT it is possible to run the same code by using different solvers by simply specifying which solver you want to run.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"24538a0a-fe23-4375-8c0c-5e9e0d8ffa72","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:47.640Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f3a569d1-3917-47c9-b77f-15bda3d39341","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"001a810d-734a-428b-be4d-b81d0c1e4e44","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"a15189ea6dd761cfe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VNsz9WqhjvcP7vPywNcT4U","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SMT user propagator theory plugin CP propagator hybrid CP-SMT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Navigating the Universe of Z3 Theory Solvers\",\"url\":\"http://theory.stanford.edu/~nikolaj/z3navigate.html\"},{\"title\":\"User-Propagation for Custom Theories in SMT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3185/extended6630.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"},{\"title\":\"IPASIR-UP: User Propagators for CDCL Katalin Fazekas # TU Wien, Austria\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"User-Propagators for Custom Theories in SMT Solving – In a Nutshell –\",\"url\":\"https://avm.sosy-lab.org/2022/prs/AVM22_Eisenhofer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ASP modulo CSP: The clingcon system⋆ Max Ostrowski and Torsten Schaub\",\"url\":\"https://research.ibm.com/haifa/Workshops/cspsat2012/papers/clingcon.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"User propagators vs. offline lemmas on demand, and clause deletion policies · Z3Prover/z3 · Discussion #7109\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Z3Prover/z3/discussions/7109\"},{\"title\":\"Developing user propagators for graph-based SMT ...\",\"url\":\"https://msp.cis.strath.ac.uk/bctcs2025/slides/critten.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Hybrid Orbit Propagator Based on Neural Networks. Multivariate Time Series Forecasting Approach | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-87869-6_66\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about SMT user propagators, theory plugins, CP propagators, and hybrid CP-SMT approaches:\n\n## User Propagators in SMT Solvers\n\nUser propagators allow callbacks to invoke propagations and detect conflicts in SMT solvers. A user propagator is an interface for customized decision procedures that uses the EUF (equality with uninterpreted functions) theory and operates in an external code-base, exposing callbacks to override Z3 behavior.\n\n## Key Applications and Use Cases\n\nUser propagators are useful when you need custom theories not directly supported by your SMT solver, encounter bad performance on large problems, use an SMT-solver as a core for your own solver, or are not happy with how SMT solvers handle certain things internally.\n\n## Integration Frameworks\n\nModular combination of theory solvers is integral to engineering modern SMT solvers, with the CDCL(T) architecture providing the overall setting for how theory solvers cooperate around a SAT solver based on conflict-driven clause learning.\n\n## Hybrid CP-SMT Approaches\n\nThe clingcon system combines the modeling language and Boolean solving of Answer Set Programming (ASP) with constraint programming (CP) techniques, with major technical innovation improving the interaction between ASP and CP solvers through elaborated learning techniques.\n\n## Recent Advances\n\nThe concept of user propagators has been introduced in the SMT solver Z3, mainly to enable users to implement custom theory support. Additionally, recent work in the context of SMT introduced an interface to seamlessly integrate a propagator for acyclicity, with evaluation on representative use cases including integrating CaDiCaL as the main CDCL(T) SAT engine in the SMT solver cvc5.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"430eb7f2-21fa-454e-96ac-e2a8faadd956","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:48.752Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"001a810d-734a-428b-be4d-b81d0c1e4e44","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
